i am glad i chased it down, tho, because i do think i have something. i kept looking at the code and something didn't sit right. so here is what i believe can happen:

imagine block `a` has a bad sig. when validating `a` the bad signature row is written into the batch table under the batch mutex. But `a`’s block id is not added to batched_ at that moment, rather it is posted later to the strand via push_batch().

before push_batch() runs, block `b` finishes and triggers batch verification. verifier sees `a`’s bad signature row, correctly marks `a` unconfirmable, and purges the table. but because `a`’s id is not yet in batched_, the invalid link cleanup cannot mark `a`’s entry as terminal.
now `a`’s delayed push_batch() finally runs and appends `a` to batched_. On the next batch, process_valids() treats every non-terminal link in batched_ as valid, so `a` can be marked valid even though it was already marked unconfirmable for an invalid signature.

